{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Your right hand, YHWH.</b> It is known that every attribute is interincluded with its counterpart, and He calls the attribute of judgment 'right hand,' because it is included and enveloped within the power of mercy — this is the sense of נאדרי בכח, from the language of אדרת (mantle). And the power of mercy within it was saving Israel, while the attribute itself, which is the attribute of judgment, was sinking the Egyptians in the sea — and this is ״ימינך ה׳ תרעץ אויב,״ and this is the illumination of what the Rabbis of blessed memory darshaned: one hand was sinking them and one hand was saving them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:22.609864150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}